{% block demo_examples %}
## Examples

The examples run on the bundled synthetic experiment, `load_ab_test()`, with its
assignment table, `load_ab_test_assignment()`, as `assignment`.

### Share of users with each transition

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.ab_transitions(
    ("exp_group", "treatment", "control"),
    assignment=assignment,
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/ab-transitions/unique-paths.html" height={640} />

90 of 92 edges are tested and 19 are black. `add_to_cart -> cart` and
`product_view -> add_to_cart` are much lower in the treatment arm, whose
`quick_add` replaces them; `cart -> cart`, a loop only the treatment arm has,
and `checkout_start -> home` are higher. `checkout_start -> payment` is grey: the
share of users with a checkout followed by a payment does not move.

### Where the transitions out of a source go

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.ab_transitions(
    ("exp_group", "treatment", "control"),
    "proba_out",
    assignment=assignment,
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/ab-transitions/proba-out.html" height={640} />

With the row-normalised weight, `checkout_start -> payment` turns blue and black
(−5.25 pp): the treatment's checkouts are more often abandoned. It is a
conditional comparison: the shortcut filled the denominator with checkouts
nobody meant to finish, while the share of users who pay after a checkout is
unchanged (the example above).
